Palm's Screen & Lock (com.palm.app.screenlock), as shipped on HP webOS 3.x.

Copyright Palm, Inc. / Hewlett-Packard. Never released under an open licence; distributed by
Lunacy as abandonware, like Mojo, the Prelude fonts and the TouchPad wallpapers: no owner has
asserted rights since webOS was discontinued.

The app is here as it was packaged, with three changes of Lunacy's, codepoet's exceptions to
rules 0 and 5: a Layout group on its main view, between the screen settings and Wallpaper,
where the owner chooses Lunacy's phone or tablet layout (Docs/phone.md; 2026-10-03), and a
"Use on Android" switch in the Wallpaper group, the opt-in to Android's own wallpaper
following webOS's (2026-10-04), and a Notifications group after Layout, where the owner chooses
apps' icons in the notifications in colour or grey, and turns on Android's notifications there by
opening Android's own Notification access screen (2026-10-16). They are the only non-Palm things in the app, marked [Lunacy]
in source/ScreenLockPrefApp.js, and talk to Lunacy's own service, not a webOS name. With it, two stylesheet rules (marked [Lunacy] in
stylesheets/screenlock.css): the view fits a phone's card, which Palm's fixed 500 px column did
not, and every footnote under a group has the same 6 px above and 9 px below. Everything else
is Palm's and runs because Lunacy answers what it asks for: com.palm.systemservice keeps its
preferences and its wallpaper, com.palm.display/control sets Android's brightness and
screen-off timeout, enyo.FilePicker finds Lunacy's picker at webOS's own path, and
com.palm.systemmanager's lock calls answer from Android's own screen lock, which Secure Unlock
sets through Android's chooser (Docs/luna-deltas.md, A21).
